{
  "id": "s04-l03",
  "unit": "s04-conjuncts",
  "title": "Conjuncts 3: shape-shifters",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Some conjuncts don't look like their parts. Learn these as whole shapes.\n\n**ক্ষ** (ক + ষ) is the most important one, and it is **not** said *ksh*. At the start of a word it's `kh` (ক্ষুধা `khudha`, *hunger*); in the middle it's a doubled `kkh` (শিক্ষক `shikkhok`, *teacher*).\n\n**ক্ত**: the ত shrinks into a little hook under ক (ডাক্তার `daktar`). **ঙ্গ** = `ngg` as in *finger* (লুঙ্গি `lunggi`). **ঞ্চ** = `nch` (পঞ্চাশ `ponchash`, *fifty*). **ষ্ট** = `sht` (মিষ্টি `mishti`, *sweet*).\n\nStrategy: if a block looks unfamiliar, check whether it's one of these five before trying to split it.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "cj-kkho",
      "bn": "ক্ষ",
      "tr": "kkho",
      "en": "kkh / kh (ক + ষ), NOT 'ksh'",
      "notes": "ক U+0995 + ্ + ষ U+09B7. At the start of a word it is just kh (ক্ষুধা khudha); in the middle it doubles (শিক্ষক shikkhok). Hindi/Sanskrit speakers: don't say ksh."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-kto",
      "bn": "ক্ত",
      "tr": "kto",
      "en": "k + t (ক + ত)",
      "notes": "ক + ্ + ত U+09A4. The ত shrinks into a hook under ক. ডাক্তার daktar, রক্ত rokto."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-nggo",
      "bn": "ঙ্গ",
      "tr": "nggo",
      "en": "ng + g (ঙ + গ), as in 'finger'",
      "notes": "ঙ U+0999 + ্ + গ U+0997. লুঙ্গি lunggi, সঙ্গে shonge."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-ncho",
      "bn": "ঞ্চ",
      "tr": "ncho",
      "en": "n + ch (ঞ + চ)",
      "notes": "ঞ U+099E + ্ + চ U+099A. পঞ্চাশ ponchash. ঞ almost always appears in this kind of cluster."
    },
    {
      "id": "cj-shto",
      "bn": "ষ্ট",
      "tr": "shto",
      "en": "sh + hard t (ষ + ট)",
      "notes": "ষ U+09B7 + ্ + ট U+099F. মিষ্টি mishti. English loans use স্ট instead (স্টেশন steshon)."
    }
  ],
